---
import ProductionLayout from '../layouts/ProductionLayout.astro';
---
<ProductionLayout title="Contact — Skyhook Industries" description="Share feedback on Expeditions or the Tether Lab, report a problem, or discuss rotating tether research and engineering collaboration with Skyhook Industries.">
  <section class="page-hero paper-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
    <h1>Tell us what you found.</h1>
    <p>A good playthrough, a confusing control, an unexpected flight result or a better engineering approach: help us make Skyhook Industries clearer, more useful and more engaging.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="paper-section">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <p class="chapter-label">01 / Contact</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Skyhook Industries</h2>
        <div class="contact-block">
          <div class="contact-line"><b>Email</b><a href="mailto:skyhookindustries@protonmail.com">skyhookindustries<wbr />@protonmail.com</a></div>
          <div class="contact-line"><b>GitHub</b><a href="https://github.com/RelyOnFire/skyhook-industries">RelyOnFire/skyhook-industries ↗</a></div>
          <div class="contact-line"><b>Project</b><span>Independent engineering study</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dark-section" id="feedback" aria-labelledby="feedback-heading">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <p class="chapter-label">02 / Game &amp; Studio feedback</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="feedback-heading">What worked? What got in the way?</h2>
        <p class="lede">Tell us what you were trying to do in Expeditions or the Tether Lab, what happened, and what you expected. Ideas, balance feedback and confusing moments are as welcome as bug reports.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">For a problem, include the page address, browser and device, plus the steps that led to it. An exact error message or screenshot helps. You can attach a campaign backup or exported Lab design if you’re comfortable sharing it; <a href="/help/">Help &amp; saves</a> explains how.</p>
        <a class="cta" href="mailto:skyhookindustries@protonmail.com?subject=Skyhook%20Industries%20feedback">Email feedback →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dark-section">
    <div class="section-grid">
      <p class="chapter-label">03 / Engineering collaboration</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Where outside expertise matters most.</h2>
        <div class="sequence">
          <div class="sequence-row"><b>A</b><strong>MATERIALS + STRUCTURES</strong><span>Allowable specific strength, fiber architectures, joints, fatigue, creep, environmental degradation and damage tolerance.</span></div>
          <div class="sequence-row"><b>B</b><strong>ORBIT + CONTROLS</strong><span>Coupled tether dynamics, post-capture transients, state estimation, deployment and recovery control.</span></div>
          <div class="sequence-row"><b>C</b><strong>CAPTURE</strong><span>Moving-target rendezvous, guidance, capture envelopes, shock attenuation, retention, release and abort logic.</span></div>
          <div class="sequence-row"><b>D</b><strong>ELECTRODYNAMICS</strong><span>Current collection, conductor architecture, Lorentz-force performance, power and orbit-dependent reboost.</span></div>
          <div class="sequence-row"><b>E</b><strong>SURVIVABILITY</strong><span>Orbital debris, micrometeoroids, inspection, repair, sectional isolation and severed-fragment trajectories.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="paper-band">
    <section class="paper-section">
      <div class="section-grid">
        <p class="chapter-label">04 / Before sending</p>
        <div>
          <h2>Keep sensitive material out of email.</h2>
          <p class="lede">Please do not send export-controlled, classified, confidential or proprietary technical information without an appropriate agreement and a secure channel.</p>
          <p class="body-copy">Public papers, published test data, open calculations, corrections to the site and pointers to relevant work are always welcome.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</ProductionLayout>
